Dump the view tree AGAIN, and say when a view controller's view moves in the hierarchy.

Two blind spots, both found while chasing why iA Writer keeps the wrong editor on screen (#194).

THE TREE DUMPED ONCE PER WINDOW, on the first displayIfNeeded. A view built in response to a CLICK
does not exist yet at that moment, so it is absent from the only tree anyone ever sees, and the
absence reads as "no such view". CIDER_VIEW_REDUMP=<seconds> dumps again, at most that often. The
once-per-window default is unchanged.

NOTHING SAID WHEN A CONTAINER SWAPPED ONE SCREENFUL FOR ANOTHER. addSubview and removeFromSuperview
now print for views that ARE a view controller's root view, which is the container swap and not
every button:

  CIDER_VIEW move addSubview <class>(<ptr>) controller=<class> other=<superview class>

WHAT IT MEASURED. iA Writer builds THREE editor stacks. The moves, in order, are one add and one
remove of A, then B added, then A again, then B four more times, then C added and removed, then B,
then C, then B three more times. B is always the last one added, so B is the one in front, and B is
the one that draws. The document goes into C. The window is not showing the editor the document was
loaded into, and the application is choosing that, not us: _insertSubview:atIndex: handles a re-add
correctly, removing the view from _subviews and re-appending it so it reorders to the front, and it
detaches from a different superview first.

That last point is worth keeping: addSubview is NOT the defect. It was checked because a duplicate
subview or a missed detach would look exactly like this from the outside.
--- a/AppKit/NSWindow.m
+++ b/AppKit/NSWindow.m
@@ -2724,8 +2724,29 @@
             if (dumped[i] == self)
                 seen = YES;
 
+        /* CIDER_VIEW_REDUMP=<seconds> DUMPS AGAIN. Once per window answers "did a layout run at
+         * all", and nothing more: a view built in response to a CLICK does not exist yet when that
+         * one dump is taken, so it is absent from the only tree anyone ever sees. iA Writer builds
+         * its third editor after a file row is clicked (#194). */
+        const char *redump = getenv("CIDER_VIEW_REDUMP");
+        NSTimeInterval every = (redump != NULL) ? (NSTimeInterval) atof(redump) : 0.0;
+
+        if (every > 0.0) {
+            static NSTimeInterval lastDump = 0.0;
+            NSTimeInterval now = [NSDate timeIntervalSinceReferenceDate];
+
+            if (now - lastDump >= every) {
+                lastDump = now;
+                seen = NO;
+            } else {
+                seen = YES;
+            }
+        }
+
         if (!seen && dumpedCount < 64) {
-            dumped[dumpedCount++] = self;
+            if (every <= 0.0) {
+                dumped[dumpedCount++] = self;
+            }
             fprintf(stderr, "CIDER_VIEW tree(displayIfNeeded) of %s title=%s\n",
                     object_getClassName(self), [[self title] UTF8String] ?: "(none)");
             fflush(stderr);
--- a/AppKit/NSView.m
+++ b/AppKit/NSView.m
@@ -1863,7 +1863,27 @@
         [self _ciderMarkNeedsConstraintSolve];
 }
 
+
+/* A CONTROLLER'S VIEW MOVING IN THE HIERARCHY, which is how one screenful is swapped for another.
+ * Only views that ARE a view controller's root view are reported, so this is the container swap and
+ * not every button. iA Writer builds a second editor for the document it opens and the window keeps
+ * the first; nothing else in the tree says whether the new one was ever offered to a superview. */
+static void _CiderNoteControllerMove(NSView *view, const char *what, NSView *other)
+{
+    if (getenv("CIDER_TRACE_VIEWS") == NULL || getenv("CIDER_TRACE_VIEWS")[0] == (char) 0)
+        return;
+    if (view == nil || view->_ciderViewController == nil)
+        return;
+
+    fprintf(stderr, "CIDER_VIEW move %s %s(%p) controller=%s other=%s\n", what,
+            object_getClassName(view), view,
+            object_getClassName(view->_ciderViewController),
+            other != nil ? object_getClassName(other) : "(nil)");
+    fflush(stderr);
+}
+
 - (void) addSubview: (NSView *) view {
+    _CiderNoteControllerMove(view, "addSubview", self);
     if (view == nil) // yes, this is silently ignored
         return;
 
@@ -2270,6 +2290,7 @@
 }
 
 - (void) removeFromSuperview {
+    _CiderNoteControllerMove(self, "removeFromSuperview", _superview);
     [_superview setNeedsDisplayInRect: [self frame]];
     [self removeFromSuperviewWithoutNeedingDisplay];
 }
